---
title: Overview
order: 1
summary: General usage, arguments and high level architecture
---


| level | queue | senders | command |
|---|---|---|---|
| threads | `LocalQueue`: `queue.Queue(C)` | M threads in one process | `sms run --level thread` |
| processes | `ProcQueue`: `multiprocessing.Queue(C)` | P processes of M threads | `sms run --level process --workers P` |
| pods | `StreamQueue`: Valkey stream `sms`, group `senders` | P pods of M threads | `sms produce`, `sms consume`, `sms monitor` |


```sh
nix develop -c just check  # checks the various things, including properties, model, spec and Jobs
sms run --level thread --senders 10 --rate 50,400,50  # rate is effectively Producer frequency, in messages per second
sms run --level process --workers 3 --senders 4  # procs
sms fold # the Summary monoid every run must reach 
```

## Param symbols throughout docs, args and frozendict


| symbol | flag | meaning | default | bounds |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| N | `--n` | messages | 1000 | 0 to 10⁹ |
| s | `--seed` | seeds every random choice | 1 | 0 to 2⁵³ − 1 |
| M | `--senders` | threads per process or pod | 10 | 1 to 10⁴ |
| C | `--capacity` | queue bound | 10 | 1 to 10⁵ |
| μ | `--mean-us` | mean attempt latency (µs) | 10⁵ | 0 to 10⁷ |
| p | `--fail-ppm` | failure probability per attempt (ppm) | 10⁵ | 0 to 10⁶ |
| A | `--attempts` | max attempts per message | 1 | 1 to 10 |
| β | `--backoff-us` | backoff base (µs) | 10⁴ | 0 to 10⁶ |
| T | `--interval-ms` | monitor period (ms) | 1000 | 100 to 60000 |
| λ | `--rate` | arrivals per second (0: closed batch) | 0 | 0 to 10⁶ |
| P | `--workers` | processes or pods | 1 | 1 to 64 |
